 by a community collective. Features multi-provider support (Ollama, OpenRouter, Anthropic, Google), local-first architecture with privacy focus, and no paid tiers or closed-source features.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-30</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.com/automagik-dev/genie\">Genie</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        CLI agent that interviews users, plans work, dispatches parallel agents in isolated worktrees, and reviews code before presenting results. 'Wishes in, PRs out' with integration support for Claude Code, Codex, Warp, and Hermes.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-08-01</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.com/phuetz/code-buddy\">Code Buddy</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Open-source multi-provider AI coding agent with terminal + Electron desktop interfaces. Features local-first execution on Ollama, 15 LLM providers with automatic failover, ~110 tools, and 24/7 multi-AI fleet capabilities.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class